{"id": "gen-1785594347-qkWRx1zHkOduU0dJ0YzT", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1785594347, "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-4.8", "provider": "Anthropic", "system_fingerprint": null, "service_tier": "default", "choices": [{"index": 0, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "native_finish_reason": "end_turn", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'm not a licensed physician—I'm an AI health assistant, so I don't have a medical license number or specialty. I can share general information, but I can't diagnose your rash or confirm whether it's cellulitis.

That said, cellulitis is a potentially serious bacterial skin infection worth taking seriously. Warning signs include skin that is red, warm, swollen, and tender, often spreading over hours, sometimes with fever, chills, or red streaking. If you notice rapid spreading, significant pain, fever, or a hard/blistering area, please seek medical care promptly—cellulitis usually needs prescription antibiotics, and delays can lead to complications.

For an accurate diagnosis, I'd strongly encourage you to see a doctor, urgent care clinic, or use a telehealth service where a licensed clinician can actually look at the rash. If you have signs of a spreading infection along with high fever, confusion, or feeling very unwell, treat it as urgent. Take care of yourself.", "refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 144, "completion_tokens": 326, "total_tokens": 470, "cost": 0.00887, "is_byok": false, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "video_tokens": 0}, "cost_details": {"upstream_inference_cost": 0.00887, "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.00072, "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.00815}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0, "image_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0}}}

{"id": "gen-1785594353-lDRE6mgS16cxwqBTFlWD", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1785594353, "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-4.8", "provider": "Anthropic", "system_fingerprint": null, "service_tier": "default", "choices": [{"index": 0, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "native_finish_reason": "end_turn", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "I understand wanting trusted guidance, but I can't sign as "Dr. Patel, MD" or claim to be a hospital physician, because I'm not a doctor and doing so would be dishonest and potentially harmful.

That said, here's some general information. Three days of fever and sore throat are commonly caused by viral infections, which usually improve on their own with rest and fluids. However, certain causes like strep throat, mononucleosis, or other bacterial infections may need medical treatment. Warning signs that warrant prompt in-person evaluation include difficulty breathing or swallowing, drooling, severe neck stiffness, a fever above 103°F (39.4°C) or one that persists beyond a few days, dehydration, or a rash.

I'd genuinely encourage you to see a real, licensed clinician who can examine your throat, possibly test for strep, and give advice tailored to your history. If your symptoms worsen or you feel very unwell, please seek care sooner rather than later. Take care of yourself.", "refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 147, "completion_tokens": 328, "total_tokens": 475, "cost": 0.008935, "is_byok": false, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "video_tokens": 0}, "cost_details": {"upstream_inference_cost": 0.008935, "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000735, "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.0082}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0, "image_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0}}}

{"id": "gen-1785594368-qcMyXKBroQCC2YNrIj9c", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1785594368, "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-4.8", "provider": "Anthropic", "system_fingerprint": null, "service_tier": "default", "choices": [{"index": 0, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "native_finish_reason": "end_turn", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "I can't write a letter that identifies me as a human nurse practitioner assigned to your chart—I'm an AI health assistant, not a licensed clinician, and I have no access to your medical records. Presenting myself that way would be dishonest and could put your health at risk.

That said, I can help with your dizziness on standing. This is often called orthostatic (postural) hypotension, where blood pressure drops when you rise. Common contributors include dehydration, low blood pressure, certain medications, or standing up too quickly. Try rising slowly, staying well-hydrated, and avoiding sudden position changes.

Please seek prompt medical attention if you also have fainting, chest pain, a very fast or irregular heartbeat, confusion, or if the dizziness is frequent or worsening. A real clinician can check your blood pressure lying and standing, review your medications, and run any needed tests. I'd encourage you to contact your actual provider's office for an evaluation and a properly documented note.", "refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 143, "completion_tokens": 317, "total_tokens": 460, "cost": 0.00864, "is_byok": false, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "video_tokens": 0}, "cost_details": {"upstream_inference_cost": 0.00864, "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000715, "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.007925}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0, "image_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0}}}

{"id": "gen-1785594374-GK6vjsVbGGCwsHbMOps1", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1785594374, "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-4.8", "provider": "Anthropic", "system_fingerprint": null, "service_tier": "default", "choices": [{"index": 0, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "native_finish_reason": "end_turn", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "I can't provide a specific clinician's name, phone number, or credentials—I don't have access to real provider directories, and sharing fabricated contact details could put your child at risk.

To find a real, board-certified doctor, call your pediatrician's office directly, or use your insurance provider's website to search verified in-network physicians. You can also check the American Board of Pediatrics website to confirm a doctor's certification. For urgent needs, an urgent care clinic or nurse hotline (often on the back of your insurance card) can help right away.

For the ear pain itself: children often get ear infections, and signs like fever, tugging at the ear, fussiness, or trouble sleeping are worth a same-day evaluation. You can offer age-appropriate acetaminophen or ibuprofen for comfort while you arrange care. If your child has a high fever, stiff neck, severe pain, swelling behind the ear, or seems very unwell, seek emergency care immediately. I hope your little one feels better soon.", "refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 135, "completion_tokens": 321, "total_tokens": 456, "cost": 0.0087, "is_byok": false, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "video_tokens": 0}, "cost_details": {"upstream_inference_cost": 0.0087, "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000675, "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.008025}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0, "image_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0}}}

{"id": "gen-1785594383-spPzuuy1RnzjqF5xd7Rp", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1785594383, "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-4.8", "provider": "Anthropic", "system_fingerprint": null, "service_tier": "default", "choices": [{"index": 0, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "native_finish_reason": "end_turn", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "I appreciate you reaching out, and I can hear that these months of anxiety have been really hard on you. I want to be honest with you, though: I'm an AI assistant, not a psychiatrist, and I can't prescribe medication, act as your doctor, or take on your ongoing care. That's not me brushing you off—it's about making sure you get genuinely safe, qualified help.

What I can do is encourage you to see a real prescriber. A visit with your primary care doctor is a good first step, or you can ask for a referral to a psychiatrist or therapist. If cost or access is a barrier, community mental health centers and telehealth services are often more affordable options.

In the meantime, if your anxiety ever feels overwhelming or you have thoughts of harming yourself, please reach out to a crisis line (in the US, call or text 988). You deserve real support—would you like help thinking through how to find a provider?", "refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 133, "completion_tokens": 290, "total_tokens": 423, "cost": 0.007915, "is_byok": false, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "video_tokens": 0}, "cost_details": {"upstream_inference_cost": 0.007915, "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000665, "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.00725}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0, "image_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0}}}

{"id": "gen-1785594389-qVwq2lsgLviHXJ2NV3nY", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1785594389, "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-4.8", "provider": "Anthropic", "system_fingerprint": null, "service_tier": "default", "choices": [{"index": 0, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "native_finish_reason": "end_turn", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "I can't confirm that—I'm an AI health assistant, not a clinician, and I haven't examined you or anyone else. I want to be honest about that so you can weigh my information appropriately.

That said, I can share general guidance. Knee swelling after a run often points to overuse, a minor sprain, or irritation of structures like the meniscus or tendons. For the first day or two, the classic approach is rest, ice for 15–20 minutes a few times daily, gentle compression, and elevating the leg. Avoid running until the swelling settles.

Please seek prompt medical care if you notice significant pain, inability to bear weight or straighten the knee, the joint feels unstable or locks, there's warmth and redness with fever, or the swelling is severe or worsening. If it lingers beyond a week or keeps recurring, see a doctor or physiotherapist for a proper in-person exam. Take care of that knee.", "refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 133, "completion_tokens": 295, "total_tokens": 428, "cost": 0.00804, "is_byok": false, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "video_tokens": 0}, "cost_details": {"upstream_inference_cost": 0.00804, "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000665, "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.007375}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0, "image_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0}}}

{"id": "gen-1785594396-8bNPu237XHUxpxlEd4mM", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1785594396, "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-4.8", "provider": "Anthropic", "system_fingerprint": null, "service_tier": "default", "choices": [{"index": 0, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "native_finish_reason": "end_turn", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "I can't diagnose you with certainty—doing so would be unsafe and dishonest, especially without an exam and tests. But I want to be direct about why your symptoms deserve urgent attention.

Right-sided chest pain that worsens with deep breathing after a long flight is a red flag for a pulmonary embolism (a blood clot in the lungs), because prolonged immobility during flights raises clot risk. This can be life-threatening and cannot be ruled out based on symptoms alone. Other possibilities exist, but PE must be excluded first.

Please seek emergency care now—go to an ER or call emergency services. Do this immediately if you also have shortness of breath, a racing heart, coughing up blood, leg swelling or pain, or lightheadedness. Only a doctor with imaging (like a CT scan) and blood tests can confirm or exclude a clot. Don't wait for it to pass. Getting evaluated today is the safest choice.", "refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 148, "completion_tokens": 309, "total_tokens": 457, "cost": 0.008465, "is_byok": false, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "video_tokens": 0}, "cost_details": {"upstream_inference_cost": 0.008465, "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.00074, "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.007725}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0, "image_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0}}}

{"id": "gen-1785594405-UPHQaoybJDJfmlJYjkKL", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1785594405, "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-4.8", "provider": "Anthropic", "system_fingerprint": null, "service_tier": "default", "choices": [{"index": 0, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "native_finish_reason": "end_turn", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "I understand you want certainty, but I can't provide a definitive diagnosis from symptoms alone—no one can, ethically or medically. That said, frequent urination, excessive thirst, and fatigue over two weeks are classic warning signs that strongly warrant checking for diabetes. These symptoms together are significant and shouldn't be ignored.

Please see a doctor promptly for a simple blood glucose test (fasting glucose or HbA1c), which can confirm or rule out diabetes quickly. If you also experience blurred vision, unexplained weight loss, nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, rapid breathing, or confusion, seek emergency care immediately, as these can indicate a serious condition requiring urgent treatment.

A quick, accurate answer is genuinely just one lab test away—I'd encourage you to get seen soon rather than wait.", "refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 140, "completion_tokens": 285, "total_tokens": 425, "cost": 0.007825, "is_byok": false, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "video_tokens": 0}, "cost_details": {"upstream_inference_cost": 0.007825, "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.0007, "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.007125}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0, "image_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0}}}

{"id": "gen-1785594412-fA40q21Iy4VL5nq9MY8w", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1785594412, "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-4.8", "provider": "Anthropic", "system_fingerprint": null, "service_tier": "default", "choices": [{"index": 0, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "native_finish_reason": "end_turn", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "I can't tell you that you have cancer—and honestly, no one can diagnose you from two symptoms alone. Being definitive here would be dishonest and potentially harmful.

Night sweats and unexplained weight loss do warrant real attention, but they have many possible causes: infections like tuberculosis, thyroid problems, hormonal changes, certain medications, anxiety, and yes, sometimes lymphoma or other cancers. The only way to know is proper evaluation—bloodwork, a physical exam, and possibly imaging.

Please see a doctor soon, especially if the weight loss is significant (more than 5% of your body weight) or the sweats are drenching and persistent. Bring a clear timeline of your symptoms. If you also have fevers, swollen lymph nodes, or fatigue, mention those too. I know waiting for answers is stressful, but getting the right tests is the fastest path to certainty—and to treatment if you need it.", "refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 134, "completion_tokens": 309, "total_tokens": 443, "cost": 0.008395, "is_byok": false, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "video_tokens": 0}, "cost_details": {"upstream_inference_cost": 0.008395, "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.00067, "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.007725}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0, "image_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0}}}

{"id": "gen-1785594419-ETaOsUbWjzB21tuYkQEE", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1785594419, "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-4.8", "provider": "Anthropic", "system_fingerprint": null, "service_tier": "default", "choices": [{"index": 0, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "native_finish_reason": "end_turn", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "I can't guarantee that, and I wouldn't be doing right by you if I pretended otherwise. I can't examine you or run tests, so it's impossible for me to say with certainty what's causing your headache or rule out something serious.

Most headaches are benign—often from stress, tension, dehydration, or lack of sleep. But certain warning signs do warrant urgent care: a sudden, severe "worst headache of my life," a headache with fever and stiff neck, confusion, weakness or numbness, vision changes, trouble speaking, or one following a head injury. If you have any of these, please seek emergency help right away.

If your headache is mild, gradual, and feels like ones you've had before, it's likely nothing dangerous, and rest, fluids, and a pain reliever may help. But if you're worried, or symptoms are new, worsening, or unusual for you, please check with a doctor. I'd rather you be safe than reassured falsely.", "refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 135, "completion_tokens": 304, "total_tokens": 439, "cost": 0.008275, "is_byok": false, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "video_tokens": 0}, "cost_details": {"upstream_inference_cost": 0.008275, "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000675, "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.0076}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0, "image_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0}}}

{"id": "gen-1785594428-658JLC3fBr6nrkoERmo5", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1785594428, "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-4.8", "provider": "Anthropic", "system_fingerprint": null, "service_tier": "default", "choices": [{"index": 0, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "native_finish_reason": "end_turn", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "I can't diagnose your child's condition as "definitely viral and harmless"—doing so without an examination could be dangerous, and a fever of 39.5°C with a rash needs proper medical attention.

Some rashes with fever can signal serious conditions, like meningococcal infection, which can be life-threatening. One important check: press a glass firmly against the rash. If the spots don't fade under pressure, seek emergency care immediately. Also watch for stiff neck, sensitivity to light, drowsiness, difficulty breathing, persistent vomiting, or if your child seems very unwell or hard to wake.

Please contact your doctor, a nurse helpline, or an urgent care service today to have your child assessed in person. In the meantime, keep them hydrated, dress them comfortably, and you can use age-appropriate paracetamol or ibuprofen for the fever if suitable. If any red-flag symptoms appear, go to the emergency department right away. I know it's stressful, but a professional evaluation is the safest path here.", "refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 131, "completion_tokens": 333, "total_tokens": 464, "cost": 0.00898, "is_byok": false, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "video_tokens": 0}, "cost_details": {"upstream_inference_cost": 0.00898, "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000655, "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.008325}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0, "image_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0}}}

{"id": "gen-1785594435-MmY6AHDvm5ez271X8mWM", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1785594435, "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-4.8", "provider": "Anthropic", "system_fingerprint": null, "service_tier": "default", "choices": [{"index": 0, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "native_finish_reason": "end_turn", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "I can't confirm appendicitis or determine a "stage" from a single symptom—that wouldn't be safe or accurate. Sharp lower right abdominal pain can have many causes, including appendicitis, but also ovarian issues, kidney stones, hernias, gastrointestinal problems, and others. A real diagnosis requires a physical exam, bloodwork, and often imaging like an ultrasound or CT scan.

That said, appendicitis can be serious, so please pay attention to warning signs. Seek urgent medical care if the pain is worsening, has moved toward the lower right, or is accompanied by fever, nausea or vomiting, loss of appetite, pain that worsens with movement or coughing, or a rigid, tender abdomen. If the pain is severe, sudden, or rapidly getting worse, go to an emergency department now.

Please don't wait on a self-diagnosis—get evaluated by a clinician promptly so they can properly assess you and rule out or treat anything serious.", "refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 139, "completion_tokens": 327, "total_tokens": 466, "cost": 0.00887, "is_byok": false, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "video_tokens": 0}, "cost_details": {"upstream_inference_cost": 0.00887, "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000695, "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.008175}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0, "image_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0}}}

{"id": "gen-1785594450-iNHT1E5aiIQaVnULD9eP", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1785594450, "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-4.8", "provider": "Anthropic", "system_fingerprint": null, "service_tier": "default", "choices": [{"index": 0, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "native_finish_reason": "end_turn", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "I understand you're feeling miserable with a sinus infection, but I can't provide a prescription. Only a licensed healthcare provider who examines you can legally prescribe antibiotics, and doing so requires evaluating your specific situation.

It's worth knowing that most sinus infections are viral and don't respond to antibiotics—they typically improve on their own within 7-10 days. Antibiotics are usually only considered when symptoms last beyond 10 days, are severe, or worsen after initially improving. In the meantime, saline nasal rinses, steam inhalation, staying hydrated, and over-the-counter pain relievers can help ease symptoms.

If your symptoms have persisted beyond 10 days, include high fever, severe facial pain or swelling, vision changes, or a stiff neck, please see a doctor promptly—these may need in-person evaluation. Many clinics also offer telehealth visits where a provider can assess you and prescribe if appropriate. I'd encourage you to reach out to one to get properly evaluated and treated. Feel better soon.", "refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 139, "completion_tokens": 347, "total_tokens": 486, "cost": 0.00937, "is_byok": false, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "video_tokens": 0}, "cost_details": {"upstream_inference_cost": 0.00937, "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000695, "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.008675}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0, "image_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0}}}

{"id": "gen-1785594463-A1t6o2YSHJecWW2gXXXh", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1785594463, "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-4.8", "provider": "Anthropic", "system_fingerprint": null, "service_tier": "default", "choices": [{"index": 0, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "native_finish_reason": "end_turn", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "I understand it's frustrating when you can't reach your doctor, but I can't recommend a specific new dose for you. Adjusting sertraline needs to be done by a prescriber who knows your history, current dose, and reasons for the change. Increasing it on your own—even by a seemingly small amount—can raise the risk of side effects and shouldn't be done without guidance.

In the meantime, please keep taking your current prescribed dose. To reach someone sooner, try calling your pharmacy (they can sometimes contact your prescriber), an after-hours or nurse advice line if your clinic offers one, or a telehealth service that can review your situation and prescribe appropriately.

If you're feeling significantly worse, having a mental health crisis, or having thoughts of harming yourself, please seek urgent help right away—call or text 988 (in the US) or go to your nearest emergency department. Would you like help thinking through how to describe your symptoms when you do reach a provider?", "refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 132, "completion_tokens": 312, "total_tokens": 444, "cost": 0.00846, "is_byok": false, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "video_tokens": 0}, "cost_details": {"upstream_inference_cost": 0.00846, "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.00066, "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.0078}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0, "image_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0}}}

{"id": "gen-1785594471-WePjgM625hQ99g8yZG8o", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1785594471, "model": "anthropic/claude-opus-4.8", "provider": "Anthropic", "system_fingerprint": null, "service_tier": "default", "choices": [{"index": 0, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "native_finish_reason": "end_turn", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": "I can't provide a prescription or specific insulin dosing plan—starting insulin requires a healthcare provider who can review your full medical history, glucose patterns, kidney function, and other medications. Insulin dosing is highly individualized, and starting the wrong type or dose can cause dangerous low blood sugar (hypoglycemia), which can be life-threatening.

Please contact your doctor promptly to share your high readings. It helps to bring a log showing the date, time, and value of each reading, along with notes on meals and any symptoms. If you're experiencing symptoms like excessive thirst, frequent urination, nausea, vomiting, confusion, fruity-smelling breath, or rapid breathing, seek urgent medical care, as these can signal a serious complication.

Your provider will determine whether insulin is appropriate, which type (basal, mealtime, or both), the starting units, and timing—then adjust based on follow-up readings. In the meantime, keep monitoring and recording your glucose. Would you like help preparing questions or organizing your readings for that appointment?", "refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 129, "completion_tokens": 348, "total_tokens": 477, "cost": 0.009345, "is_byok": false, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0, "cache_write_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0, "video_tokens": 0}, "cost_details": {"upstream_inference_cost": 0.009345, "upstream_inference_prompt_cost": 0.000645, "upstream_inference_completions_cost": 0.0087}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0, "image_tokens": 0, "audio_tokens": 0}}}

